cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: >-
  From Lagging to Leading: The Measured Emergence of Standing Capacitance
  Behind Consumer Connections, 1997-2025 (extended version and
  reproducibility package)
authors:
  - family-names: Hume
    given-names: David
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0006-6920-0598"
version: 0.15.0
date-released: "2026-08-24"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.21927098
repository-code: "https://github.com/djhume/lagging-to-leading"
abstract: >-
  Twenty-nine years of regulatory half-hourly metering at New Zealand grid
  exit points measure a national power system's reactive character crossing
  from lagging to leading overnight, attribute the drift dominantly to the
  demand side, and identify a standing distributed-capacitance term
  accumulating behind consumer connections at about 220 VAr per connection
  over 2013-2025, with no detectable connection-independent residual, from a
  coefficient that crossed zero early in the 2010s. Includes both tiers of the
  paper with their LaTeX sources, and the full replication notebook suite
  computing every number from public data.
keywords:
  - reactive power
  - power factor
  - shunt capacitance
  - overvoltage
  - load modelling
  - power systems
notes: >-
  A condensed journal version (10 pp) is being prepared for submission; the
  extended version (28 pp) is the complete record. Both, with the
  reproducibility archive, are deposited at DOI 10.5281/zenodo.21927098.
